*** Add File:helm/cosign-admission/README_KMS_TLS.md
+# Cosign Admission — KMS & TLS setup (operator steps)
+
+1) Provision KMS key (AWS example using Terraform)
+   - terraform init && terraform apply -var 'aws_region=us-west-2'
+   - Copy output "cosign_kms_key_arn"
+
+2) Store KMS ARN in Kubernetes secret
+   - ./ops/cosign/attach_kms_secret.sh <KMS_KEY_ARN> security
+
+3) TLS for webhook (cert-manager recommended)
+   - Install cert-manager in the cluster.
+   - Create Issuer or ClusterIssuer for your CA.
+   - Create a Certificate resource for the cosign-admission service:
+     apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
+     kind: Certificate
+     metadata:
+       name: cosign-admission-cert
+       namespace: admission
+     spec:
+       secretName: cosign-webhook-tls
+       dnsNames:
+         - cosign-admission.admission.svc
+       issuerRef:
+         name: <issuer-name>
+         kind: ClusterIssuer
+
+4) Populate CA bundle into ValidatingWebhookConfiguration
+   - After certificate issued, run:
+     ./ops/cosign/populate_ca_bundle.sh admission cosign-webhook-tls cosign-validating-webhook
+
+5) CI wiring (GitHub Actions)
+   - Add COSIGN_AWS_KMS_KEY_ARN secret to GitHub Actions; CI will sign artifacts using cosign with this KMS key.
+
