*** Add File:services/rl/policy/evolution_plan.md
+# RL Policy Evolution Plan: safe-to-apply progression
+
+This plan formalizes how candidates from the RL sandbox are advanced toward controlled automation:
+
+Stage 0 — Sandbox evaluation (continuous)
+ - Candidates generated and offline-evaluated with offline_eval.py across multiple trace slices.
+ - Candidates with estimated reward above configured threshold (e.g., +5% cost saving with <0.5% quality degradation) promoted to Stage 1 queue.
+
+Stage 1 — Human-in-the-loop apply (manual)
+ - Operators request application via manual-approval service using safe_apply_operator.
+ - Each applied policy is monitored for at least 7 days; detailed metrics (acceptance_rate, verifier precision, fallback rate) are collected.
+
+Stage 2 — Controlled canary automation (limited automation)
+ - If Stage 1 results are acceptable for at least 3 distinct candidates, small automated canary windows are allowed (1% traffic, 24h).
+ - Automation allowed only if policy constraints from safe_policy.json are satisfied.
+
+Stage 3 — Progressive automation (time gated)
+ - Gradually increase automated rollout if no regressions and SMEs sign off.
+ - Always maintain manual override and audit logs.
+
+Safety guarantees:
+ - All RL actions must be reversible via promotion-backup configmap rollback.
+ - Circuit breaker auto-disables RL actions when verifier precision drops or acceptance_rate falls below thresholds.
+
